# Composition over inheritance

- **Inheritance = "is-a"
- **Composition = "has-a"

```java
private final Repository repo;                 // has-a
public void place(Order o) { repo.save(o); }   // delegate
```

## Why inheritance disappoints for reuse

- **Rigid** — inherit everything, locked to one superclass
- **Fragile base class** — an upstream change silently breaks you
- **Leaks the whole surface** — `extends ArrayList` exposes `add`, `remove`…

```java
public class Stack<T> {
    private final List<T> items = new ArrayList<>();   // hidden
    public void push(T x) { items.add(x); }
    public T pop() { return items.remove(items.size() - 1); }
}
```
